        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 888 7th Avenue, 200 West Street, Midtown Manhattan, Lower Manhattan, New York\n- Companies: Goldman Sachs, Pershing Square Capital Management\n- People: Bill Ackman\n- Topics: office skyscrapers, headquarters, hedge fund management\n\nFacts:\n- 888 7th Avenue was completed in 1969 as a modern-style office skyscraper in Midtown Manhattan.\n- 888 7th Avenue is 628 feet tall, 46 floors high, and located in Midtown Manhattan.\n- 200 West Street is a 749-foot, 44-story building on West Street between Vesey Street and Murray Street in Lower Manhattan.\n- 200 West Street serves as the global headquarters of Goldman Sachs.\n- Pershing Square Capital Management is an American hedge fund management company founded and run by Bill Ackman.\n- Pershing Square Capital Management is located at 888 7th Avenue in New York.",
